# Environment for riptide.service (systemd EnvironmentFile syntax).
#
# JVM options:
#JAVA_OPTS=-Xmx2g
#
# Any riptide.* property can also be set as an environment variable here
# (Spring relaxed binding), e.g.:
#RIPTIDE_CLICKHOUSE_ENDPOINT=http://clickhouse.example.com:8123
#
# Continuous profiling to a Pyroscope server. Off by default.
# See the operator docs, "Continuous profiling": https://riptide.space/docs/deploy/operations
#
# Uncomment all three together.
#
# Set the server address explicitly. Leave it out and the agent falls back to
# http://localhost:4040, which starts cleanly and logs "Continuous profiling
# started" while every profile goes nowhere. There is no error to notice.
#
# The flag is needed because the agent loads a native library. JDK 25 only
# warns; a future release blocks it, and then profiling stops. That failure is
# logged and the collector keeps running, so you lose the profile and nothing
# else. Note it does not silence the separate sun.misc.Unsafe warning the agent
# also produces, which is upstream's to fix; the docs above explain why.
#
# JAVA_OPTS is a single assignment and the last one wins, so carry every option
# on one line. Replace the commented -Xmx line above rather than adding to it.
#RIPTIDE_PROFILING_ENABLED=true
#PYROSCOPE_SERVER_ADDRESS=http://pyroscope.internal:4040
#JAVA_OPTS=-Xmx2g --enable-native-access=ALL-UNNAMED
